      "peer_disclosure_id": "amd_2024_1A_D065",
      "relationship": "related_topic",
      "comparison": "Both NVIDIA and AMD disclose risks related to their reliance on overseas supply chains, but NVIDIA specifically highlights the geopolitical risk of restrictions impacting Taiwan, whereas AMD focuses on the broader operational risk of third-party component and AIB partner support. NVIDIA explicitly states that 'Any new restrictions that negatively impact our ability to receive supply of components, parts, or services from Taiwan, would negatively impact our business and financial results,' indicating a direct vulnerability to political/export controls. In contrast, AMD discloses that 'If the designers, manufacturers, AIBs and suppliers of motherboards, graphics cards, software, memory and other components cease or reduce their design, manufacture or production... our business could be materially adversely affected,' focusing on commercial or functional cessation rather than geopolitical restriction as the primary cited mechanism for disruption.",
      "target_sentence_ids": [
        "nvda_2024_1A_P081_S002"
      ],
