        "amd_2024_1A_P064_S005"
      ]
    },
    {
      "peer_ticker": "AVGO",
      "peer_disclosure_id": "avgo_2024_1A_D018",
      "relationship": "no_match",
      "reason": "The candidate disclosure concerns software product acceptance risk, which is unrelated to NVIDIA's supply chain and overseas partner reliance."
    },
    {
      "peer_ticker": "INTC",
      "peer_disclosure_id": "intc_2024_1A_D014",
      "relationship": "same_topic",
      "comparison": "Intel and NVIDIA both explicitly identify Taiwan as a critical location for their supply chains and cite geopolitical tensions and hostilities as specific risks that could disrupt the supply of components. NVIDIA states its business depends on 'reliable supply from our overseas partners, especially in Taiwan' and risks from 'new restrictions... from Taiwan.' Similarly, Intel notes that 'Many of our products and all of our more advanced products depend on suppliers in Taiwan for critical components... that cannot be easily or quickly replaced' and that 'Tensions between mainland China and Taiwan have increased significantly... presenting an elevated risk of hostilities.' Both companies frame the risk around the inability to quickly replace supply if Taiwan is impacted by conflict or restrictions.",
      "target_sentence_ids": [
        "nvda_2024_1A_P081_S001"
      ],
      "peer_sentence_ids": [
        "intc_2024_1A_P033_S004"
      ]
    },
    {
      "peer_ticker": "MU",
      "peer_disclosure_id": "mu_2024_1A_D017",
      "relationship": "same_topic",
      "comparison": "Micron and NVIDIA both disclose that a significant portion of their production relies on Taiwan and that political or economic actions affecting Taiwan pose a material risk to their business. NVIDIA highlights reliance on 'overseas partners, especially in Taiwan' and the negative impact of 'new restrictions' on supply. Micron explicitly states that 'A majority of our DRAM production output in 2024 was from our fabrication facilities in Taiwan, and any loss of output could have a material adverse effect on us,' and that 'political, economic, or other actions may adversely affect our operations in Taiwan.' Both companies identify Taiwan production concentration and the specific threat of political/economic disruption as a key supply chain risk.",
      "target_sentence_ids": [
        "nvda_2024_1A_P081_S001"
      ],
      "peer_sentence_ids": [
        "mu_2024_1A_P020_S002"
      ]
    },
    {
      "peer_ticker": "QCOM",
      "peer_disclosure_id": "qcom_2024_1A_D093",
      "relationship": "same_topic",
      "comparison": "Qualcomm and NVIDIA both identify geopolitical tensions involving China and Taiwan as a risk that could disrupt their supply chains. NVIDIA notes that 'new restrictions' impacting supply from Taiwan would negatively affect its business. Qualcomm discloses that 'geopolitical tensions involving China and Taiwan' could 'delay or prevent our suppliers from providing us with critical components' and 'delaying or preventing our foundry... providers from manufacturing, assembling or testing our products.' Both companies link the specific geopolitical conflict in the Taiwan region directly to the potential failure or delay of their semiconductor supply chain.",
      "target_sentence_ids": [
        "nvda_2024_1A_P081_S002"
      ],
      "peer_sentence_ids": [
        "qcom_2024_1A_P120_S003"
      ]
    }
